# General agent guidance

Before substantial changes, read:

- [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) — architecture and conventions
- [docs/development-workflow.md](../../docs/development-workflow.md) — step-by-step workflow
- [docs/overview.md](../../docs/overview.md) — product scope and current milestone

## Preserve existing choices

Do not replace Ruff, pre-commit, Alembic, FastAPI layout, or Docker Compose without a concrete technical problem.

## Scope

- Smallest correct diff; no unrelated edits
- No new dependencies unless necessary
- English for all code, identifiers, and comments
- Never commit secrets (`.env`, credentials, tokens)

## Quality

- Backend: `pre-commit-run` when applicable. `typecheck` and `test` run in Docker.
- Game engine / rules evaluator: `lint-couple-simulator-engine`, `test-couple-simulator-engine`, `lint-rules-evaluator`, `test-rules-evaluator` run in Docker (Python 3.12). Do not use host `pip` for those targets.
- Use `make <target>` or `./task.sh <target>` if `make` is missing.
- Frontend: `lint-frontend`, `format-check-frontend`, and `build-check-frontend` run in Docker. Do not use host `npm` for those targets. Same `make` / `./task.sh` choice.
- Tell the user which migration commands to run; do not run DB operations yourself

See [docs/backlog/engineering-baseline-backlog.md](../../docs/backlog/engineering-baseline-backlog.md) for planned CI and deployment work.
